# R96E1 receipt — item 4: before-witness (round-95 instruments under the same shim)
#
# The F1 defect named in plans/round-96.plan.md is a property of the CHECKER, not of
# the C1 counter: every measure-*.py in this lane (round 94 at 6a2a1fdd, round 95 at
# the base, round 96 at the freeze) invokes git through sealed_env() with
# PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin. The round-95 checker
# (.ufo/evidence/round-95/conjunct-disposition-v95.py at base c8de77f3, sha256
# d6cf94b4...) builds its environment as `os.environ` minus GIT_*, i.e. it KEEPS the
# inherited PATH, and it reads the counter, the manifest and every receipt with
# `git cat-file` / `git ls-tree`. The receipts below reproduce F1 on those bytes,
# then run the successor checker (.ufo/evidence/round-96/conjunct-disposition-v96.py
# at the freeze, sha256 6c38dacd...) against the same lane, shim and forged directory.
#
# Lane for the checker runs: clone-honest (shared clone) checked out at the freeze rev.
# The audited rev has ZERO committed receipts:
#   $ git -C clone-honest ls-tree -r --name-only be6c22b6... -- \
#         .ufo/evidence/round-96/pre-freeze/controls
#   (no output; the same query at base c8de77f3 also prints nothing)
# The forged directory forge-all holds:
#   .ufo/evidence/round-96/c1/measure-v96.py      = the committed counter (e0da9935...)
#   .ufo/evidence/round-96/conjunct-disposition.json = the committed freeze manifest
#                                                      (sha256 31e4667b...)
#   .ufo/evidence/round-96/pre-freeze/controls/*.out = 16 receipts copied from
#       c8de77f3:.ufo/evidence/round-95/pre-freeze/controls/<state>.out with the first
#       `counter_sha=` line rewritten to e0da9935... (the counter blob at the audited
#       rev), so a checker that accepts them accepts bytes the audited lane never held.
#   _listings/.ufo_evidence_round-96_pre-freeze_controls.ls = the matching ls-tree listing.
#
# Part A: round-95 checker (v95 bytes, base c8de77f3): honest PATH vs hostile PATH.
# Part B: checker at 6a2a1fdd (v94 bytes) — the plan's literal revision — on the
#   freeze rev (receipts exist only in the WORKING TREE, zero committed) and on the
#   base rev (counter+manifest absent at rev; the shim supplies them).
# Part C: successor checker (v96 at the freeze): same lane, same shim.
# Part D: the round-94 counter blob at 6a2a1fdd under the same shim (the seat spec's
#   "round-95 counter ... C1_R94_PASS=true" sentence): measured on the honest lane
#   and on the forged lane. The shim log is absent in both; the counter is already
#   PATH-sealed, so the sentence's PASS=true instance is the honest pass, not a forgery.

######## Part A: round-95 checker (v95 bytes at base) — F1 reproduced ########
