# shim-v94counter-a.log / -b.log: ABSENT (0 calls) in both runs. So D1's
# C1_R94_PASS=true is the honest pass on the honest lane (the counter read the
# committed note), not a forged green; D2's C1_R94_PASS=false is the same counter
# refusing the forged lane while a PATH-resolving reader would have been handed the
# honest note. The old counter is already PATH-sealed (measure-v94.py lines 101-112:
# sealed_env() pins PATH and git() passes env=), so the F1 forgery is a property of
# the CHECKER (Parts A-B), not of the counter.


######## Part E: context — the successor checker's rev tokens (independent measurement) ########
# The plan's C1 wording claims exit 2 + `rev-not-a-commit-id` for any non-40-hex
# --rev and exit 2 + `rev-unresolvable` for a 40-hex id that does not resolve.
