# `git rev-parse <40hex>` exits 0 for a syntactically valid name that is not an
# object (see R96E1-rev-refusals.out Part C), so `rev-unresolvable` is unreachable
# on that path; and an empty --rev is caught by the usage check (exit 64) before
# the shape guard. Both refusals still refuse (exit 2/64, never green).
